verdict.reasoning:
I tried to refute both halves of the claim, and both hold.

1) Full-run gating. The shipped config.json retrieval block has only the keys archives, frames_root, mode and scratch_dir. config3b.py does not require fidelity_check when mode is fetch, and retrieve() never checks for an earlier passing fidelity record. The full run would therefore fetch and sparse-extract all 290 videos, mark every input "ok", and pass them to baseline. Its own records would hold no fidelity evidence.

The engineering brief (VERA_Fixed_Adaptive_Workflow_Handoff.md:83) says: "extract only needed frames when fidelity checks pass". PROTOCOL §3.1 and §10 meet this only through the separate integration run. Nothing links that run to the full run. The fidelity_check output also does not record cv2_version, so the two environments cannot be compared afterwards.

2) Coverage. tests/ never references acquire3b, sparse_extract or fidelity (grep returns exit 1). synthetic.py uses retrieval.mode 'none'. config.integration.json uses 'existing_only'. The integration run does exercise _fetch_member, sparse_extract and _purge through fidelity_check(). It never exercises the per-video fetch branch of retrieve(), lines 222-269:
- writing the identity file;
- the fps and count metadata flags;
- _apply_identity;
- purging fetched copies;
- the local-video branch;
- skipping on resume via the identity file.

Mitigating facts:
- The integration check and the full run would use the same pinned conda environment on oz, so a different decoder build is a speculative scenario.
- The full run has not been launched.
- My stub run of the fetch branch worked: identity files written, statuses ok, scratch purged.
So this is a real but minor gap in a stated requirement, not a wrong result in current outputs.

One correction to the reviewer's fix. Adding fidelity_check to config.json would NOT verify "before extracting". retrieve() runs fidelity_check at line 272, after the per-video loop. The check would therefore stop the baseline and later stages: retrieve raises, inputs.json is not written, the stage is marked failed and later stages are skipped. But the check would only fire after all ~8 GB of downloads and all 3464 frames had been written. The identity files would persist, and the in-memory statuses would still read "ok".

